UPAS-X demonstrates that multi-body shadow geometry, relativistic ephemerides, 
and HDR flux fields can be simulated at unprecedented spatial scales with 
high numerical stability. The architecture provides a foundation for future 
extensions including exoplanet transit modeling, stellar photometry, and 
multi-body gravitational systems.

